1
00:00:00,316 --> 00:00:02,644
I'm shocked at how few
people actually

2
00:00:02,644 --> 00:00:05,662
know why their knee
replacement still hurts.

3
00:00:05,899 --> 00:00:07,763
They have no idea what's
actually

4
00:00:07,763 --> 00:00:09,634
happening inside their new
knee.

5
00:00:09,942 --> 00:00:10,956
The new knee is not

6
00:00:10,956 --> 00:00:12,022
actually a new knee

7
00:00:12,022 --> 00:00:13,464
in the way that you think.

8
00:00:13,743 --> 00:00:15,705
The surgeon replaces the
worn-out ends

9
00:00:15,705 --> 00:00:17,000
of the bones with smooth

10
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:19,297
metal caps and a plastic
spacer,

11
00:00:19,297 --> 00:00:21,035
and everything around them
is still

12
00:00:21,035 --> 00:00:23,320
the same living tissue
you've always had.

13
00:00:23,549 --> 00:00:24,666
To put the new parts

14
00:00:24,666 --> 00:00:25,700
in, the surgeon has

15
00:00:25,700 --> 00:00:27,236
to work through that
tissue,

16
00:00:27,236 --> 00:00:28,492
the joint capsule,

17
00:00:28,492 --> 00:00:30,695
its soft inner lining
called the synovium,

18
00:00:30,695 --> 00:00:32,450
and the padding wrapped
around

19
00:00:32,450 --> 00:00:33,672
the front of your knee.

20
00:00:33,812 --> 00:00:36,322
That tissue folds and
slides every time

21
00:00:36,322 --> 00:00:38,145
you bend and straighten,
just

22
00:00:38,145 --> 00:00:40,277
like the folds of an
accordion

23
00:00:40,277 --> 00:00:42,505
opening and closing around
the joint.

24
00:00:42,717 --> 00:00:44,531
It cushions the new joint
and

25
00:00:44,531 --> 00:00:45,813
tells your brain where

26
00:00:45,813 --> 00:00:47,414
your leg is with every
step,

27
00:00:47,414 --> 00:00:48,186
so you

28
00:00:48,186 --> 00:00:50,169
can walk without thinking
about it.

29
00:00:50,763 --> 00:00:52,199
But here's the crazy part.

30
00:00:52,301 --> 00:00:54,584
These new joints are so
well made

31
00:00:54,584 --> 00:00:56,206
that most of them are
expected

32
00:00:56,206 --> 00:00:57,920
to last twenty years or
more.

33
00:00:58,173 --> 00:00:59,305
It's amazing.

34
00:00:59,571 --> 00:01:01,923
However, because the
tissue around

35
00:01:01,923 --> 00:01:03,778
it isn't metal or plastic,

36
00:01:03,778 --> 00:01:05,402
this means that after
surgery

37
00:01:05,402 --> 00:01:07,513
it gets swollen and
irritated,

38
00:01:07,513 --> 00:01:09,043
and in some people it
doesn't

39
00:01:09,043 --> 00:01:10,101
calm back down the way

40
00:01:10,101 --> 00:01:11,428
the metal settles in.

41
00:01:11,579 --> 00:01:13,947
Sadly, about one in five

42
00:01:13,947 --> 00:01:15,563
people with a knee
replacement

43
00:01:15,563 --> 00:01:17,630
keep hurting long after
surgery,

44
00:01:17,630 --> 00:01:20,245
while most people's tissue
calms down,

45
00:01:20,245 --> 00:01:21,269
so they never feel

46
00:01:21,269 --> 00:01:22,811
it as the months go by.

47
00:01:23,045 --> 00:01:24,740
It's just some of us who
have

48
00:01:24,740 --> 00:01:26,941
to deal with it, and the
neighbor

49
00:01:26,941 --> 00:01:28,655
who was golfing at three

50
00:01:28,655 --> 00:01:30,512
months will never
understand.

51
00:01:30,612 --> 00:01:32,530
And you've probably
already noticed

52
00:01:32,530 --> 00:01:34,313
that it isn't really a
sharp pain.

53
00:01:34,496 --> 00:01:35,730
It's a tightness.

54
00:01:35,900 --> 00:01:36,875
A pressure.

55
00:01:37,167 --> 00:01:38,684
Like an invisible band

56
00:01:38,684 --> 00:01:39,957
wrapped around the knee.

57
00:01:40,236 --> 00:01:42,126
This means getting out of
the car

58
00:01:42,126 --> 00:01:44,217
or up off the couch is
harder

59
00:01:44,217 --> 00:01:45,929
than walking on flat
ground,

60
00:01:45,929 --> 00:01:47,938
because those bend the
knee the most.

61
00:01:48,278 --> 00:01:49,281
But it's also why

62
00:01:49,281 --> 00:01:50,499
it can ache at night,

63
00:01:50,499 --> 00:01:52,232
when you're lying
perfectly still.

64
00:01:52,720 --> 00:01:54,467
Deep bends like sitting
down into

65
00:01:54,467 --> 00:01:55,843
a car seat or lowering

66
00:01:55,843 --> 00:01:57,501
yourself onto the toilet

67
00:01:57,501 --> 00:01:58,709
squeeze much harder than

68
00:01:58,709 --> 00:02:00,022
a small bend like

69
00:02:00,022 --> 00:02:01,989
a slow walk across the
kitchen.

70
00:02:02,283 --> 00:02:03,736
You can try it for
yourself.

71
00:02:04,094 --> 00:02:05,104
Just bend your knee back

72
00:02:05,104 --> 00:02:06,295
as far as it will go,

73
00:02:06,295 --> 00:02:08,118
then straighten it all the
way out,

74
00:02:08,118 --> 00:02:09,391
and compare it to a small

75
00:02:09,391 --> 00:02:10,712
easy bend in the middle.

76
00:02:11,010 --> 00:02:12,583
You can probably feel that
the two

77
00:02:12,583 --> 00:02:14,497
ends are much tighter than
the middle.

78
00:02:14,779 --> 00:02:16,868
And the problem is when
the knee

79
00:02:16,868 --> 00:02:18,473
tightens up at both ends,

80
00:02:18,473 --> 00:02:19,880
it doesn't just mean you
lose

81
00:02:19,880 --> 00:02:21,759
a few degrees here and
there.

82
00:02:21,857 --> 00:02:22,687
No,

83
00:02:22,687 --> 00:02:24,952
it means you stop trusting
the knee

84
00:02:24,952 --> 00:02:27,876
to carry you without
checking it first.

85
00:02:28,107 --> 00:02:29,653
So even if you can still

86
00:02:29,653 --> 00:02:30,826
do most of the things

87
00:02:30,826 --> 00:02:32,509
you used to do,

88
00:02:32,509 --> 00:02:34,769
it's like you lost your
autopilot.

89
00:02:35,152 --> 00:02:36,179
When you walk,

90
00:02:36,179 --> 00:02:37,896
you're not actually
thinking about

91
00:02:37,896 --> 00:02:39,687
every single step you
take.

92
00:02:39,967 --> 00:02:41,895
Your brain is constantly
feeling

93
00:02:41,895 --> 00:02:43,064
the ground and

94
00:02:43,064 --> 00:02:45,729
predicting and adjusting
to kind of fill

95
00:02:45,729 --> 00:02:47,513
in the blanks all the
time.

96
00:02:47,884 --> 00:02:49,581
That's how you're able to
walk

97
00:02:49,581 --> 00:02:51,749
and talk at the same time,

98
00:02:51,749 --> 00:02:53,506
and why even if the
sidewalk

99
00:02:53,506 --> 00:02:55,121
is uneven or you step off

100
00:02:55,121 --> 00:02:56,617
a curb you didn't see,

101
00:02:56,617 --> 00:02:57,981
your body can still catch

102
00:02:57,981 --> 00:02:59,528
itself pretty easily.

103
00:02:59,876 --> 00:03:01,401
But when the knee feels
squeezed,

104
00:03:01,401 --> 00:03:03,539
you lose so much of that
trust

105
00:03:03,539 --> 00:03:05,543
every time it tightens on
a bend.

106
00:03:05,894 --> 00:03:07,786
And now you actually have
to think

107
00:03:07,786 --> 00:03:10,401
about every step and plan
every move

108
00:03:10,401 --> 00:03:12,003
just to get where you're
going.

109
00:03:12,371 --> 00:03:13,391
This is why you find

110
00:03:13,391 --> 00:03:15,063
it so much more tiring to
go

111
00:03:15,063 --> 00:03:16,425
out than you used to.

112
00:03:16,793 --> 00:03:18,084
Walking when your knee
feels

113
00:03:18,084 --> 00:03:19,863
right is a passive
process.

114
00:03:19,986 --> 00:03:22,058
You just do it without
thinking.

115
00:03:22,320 --> 00:03:24,319
But when your knee feels
squeezed,

116
00:03:24,319 --> 00:03:26,113
if you want to go
somewhere,

117
00:03:26,113 --> 00:03:28,496
you have to actively put
in effort.

118
00:03:28,863 --> 00:03:30,558
You do the parking lot
math before

119
00:03:30,558 --> 00:03:31,919
you get out of the car.

120
00:03:32,151 --> 00:03:33,389
You take the stairs one

121
00:03:33,389 --> 00:03:34,317
at a time.

122
00:03:34,519 --> 00:03:35,702
You learn where the chairs

123
00:03:35,702 --> 00:03:37,263
are in every store.

124
00:03:37,544 --> 00:03:38,672
It's stressful

125
00:03:38,672 --> 00:03:39,913
and it's exhausting.

126
00:03:40,159 --> 00:03:41,562
And a lot of that is down

127
00:03:41,562 --> 00:03:43,052
to the tissue being
squeezed.

128
00:03:43,153 --> 00:03:44,930
So why is it that the
tightness

129
00:03:44,930 --> 00:03:46,319
is worst when you bend?

130
00:03:46,530 --> 00:03:48,289
Well, your new knee sits

131
00:03:48,289 --> 00:03:49,970
inside a fixed space,

132
00:03:49,970 --> 00:03:51,881
and the swollen tissue
around it

133
00:03:51,881 --> 00:03:53,876
takes up more room than it
should.

134
00:03:54,238 --> 00:03:56,216
Think about what happens
when your foot

135
00:03:56,216 --> 00:03:57,683
swells inside a shoe.

136
00:03:57,963 --> 00:03:58,986
The shoe didn't shrink,

137
00:03:58,986 --> 00:04:00,720
but everything starts to
feel

138
00:04:00,720 --> 00:04:01,860
cramped and tight.

139
00:04:02,141 --> 00:04:04,642
So when you bend your
knee,

140
00:04:04,642 --> 00:04:06,372
that swollen tissue gets
squeezed,

141
00:04:06,372 --> 00:04:08,485
and when you straighten
it,

142
00:04:08,485 --> 00:04:10,036
it gets pulled tight,

143
00:04:10,036 --> 00:04:11,299
with less and less room

144
00:04:11,299 --> 00:04:12,266
as it does.

145
00:04:12,433 --> 00:04:13,613
It's just like your foot

146
00:04:13,613 --> 00:04:14,460
in that shoe.

147
00:04:14,603 --> 00:04:15,603
The more it swells,

148
00:04:15,603 --> 00:04:17,312
the tighter every step
gets.

149
00:04:17,576 --> 00:04:18,257
So what

150
00:04:18,257 --> 00:04:19,482
can we do about it?

151
00:04:19,829 --> 00:04:21,874
Well, let's look at what
usually happens

152
00:04:21,874 --> 00:04:24,103
when a knee replacement
still hurts,

153
00:04:24,103 --> 00:04:25,401
because for years,

154
00:04:25,401 --> 00:04:26,644
the main answer has been

155
00:04:26,644 --> 00:04:27,750
to quiet down the pain

156
00:04:27,750 --> 00:04:29,567
signal coming out of the
knee.

157
00:04:29,734 --> 00:04:31,230
It started with pain pills
you'd take

158
00:04:31,230 --> 00:04:33,664
every morning to take the
edge off.

159
00:04:34,101 --> 00:04:35,445
Then came the nerve block,

160
00:04:35,445 --> 00:04:36,786
a needle near the nerves

161
00:04:36,786 --> 00:04:38,001
around the knee to switch

162
00:04:38,001 --> 00:04:39,771
the signal off for a
while.

163
00:04:40,015 --> 00:04:40,904
And over time,

164
00:04:40,904 --> 00:04:42,384
we went from a pill that
lasts

165
00:04:42,384 --> 00:04:44,582
a few hours to nerve
ablation,

166
00:04:44,582 --> 00:04:46,523
where a doctor uses heat
to quiet

167
00:04:46,523 --> 00:04:48,949
the nerve that carries the
pain.

168
00:04:48,989 --> 00:04:49,729
For many years,

169
00:04:49,729 --> 00:04:51,802
the only real advancements
were seeing how

170
00:04:51,802 --> 00:04:52,834
long the quiet could last

171
00:04:52,834 --> 00:04:54,453
before the pain came back.

172
00:04:54,816 --> 00:04:57,067
But there was still a huge
problem,

173
00:04:57,067 --> 00:04:58,806
and that problem is the
reason why

174
00:04:58,806 --> 00:05:00,590
so many people go through
every

175
00:05:00,590 --> 00:05:02,331
one of these and still
hurt.

176
00:05:02,605 --> 00:05:04,253
So, what's the problem?

177
00:05:04,568 --> 00:05:07,063
Well, as we talked about
before,

178
00:05:07,063 --> 00:05:07,905
the new knee sits

179
00:05:07,905 --> 00:05:08,998
in a fixed space,

180
00:05:08,998 --> 00:05:10,102
and the tissue around

181
00:05:10,102 --> 00:05:11,376
it is swollen and

182
00:05:11,376 --> 00:05:13,315
taking up more room than
it should.

183
00:05:13,656 --> 00:05:15,908
Your body has spent your
entire life

184
00:05:15,908 --> 00:05:17,813
learning how your knee
should feel,

185
00:05:17,813 --> 00:05:19,564
and now that squeeze sends
a warning

186
00:05:19,564 --> 00:05:21,362
every single time you
bend.

187
00:05:21,582 --> 00:05:22,504
In fact,

188
00:05:22,504 --> 00:05:24,561
the pain signal is often
the only

189
00:05:24,561 --> 00:05:26,238
part of this anyone
treats.

190
00:05:26,516 --> 00:05:28,462
The nerve is just the
messenger,

191
00:05:28,462 --> 00:05:29,876
but the message keeps
coming

192
00:05:29,876 --> 00:05:31,510
from the same swollen
tissue.

193
00:05:31,773 --> 00:05:33,313
So these treatments would
just

194
00:05:33,313 --> 00:05:34,655
quiet the signal,

195
00:05:34,655 --> 00:05:36,651
exactly like turning down
the volume

196
00:05:36,651 --> 00:05:37,936
on a smoke alarm.

197
00:05:38,314 --> 00:05:39,576
But the problem is,

198
00:05:39,576 --> 00:05:41,100
the smoke is still there.

199
00:05:41,369 --> 00:05:42,926
And because nothing went
near

200
00:05:42,926 --> 00:05:44,282
the swollen tissue,

201
00:05:44,282 --> 00:05:46,320
every bend still squeezes
it,

202
00:05:46,320 --> 00:05:48,478
and it sends the same
message again

203
00:05:48,478 --> 00:05:49,472
the next morning.

204
00:05:49,687 --> 00:05:50,846
The pills and the needles

205
00:05:50,846 --> 00:05:52,333
made the knee quieter,

206
00:05:52,333 --> 00:05:53,576
but they did nothing about

207
00:05:53,576 --> 00:05:54,905
what was making the noise

208
00:05:54,905 --> 00:05:56,107
in the first place.

209
00:05:56,424 --> 00:05:58,110
And this is why the tissue
itself

210
00:05:58,110 --> 00:05:59,473
has to be the target.

211
00:05:59,644 --> 00:06:00,938
It's not enough to just

212
00:06:00,938 --> 00:06:01,996
quiet the signal.

213
00:06:02,373 --> 00:06:03,855
What actually helps

214
00:06:03,855 --> 00:06:06,431
is calming the irritated
tissue,

215
00:06:06,431 --> 00:06:08,033
so that it takes up less
room

216
00:06:08,033 --> 00:06:09,703
and the pressure comes
down.

217
00:06:10,025 --> 00:06:11,886
That means whatever you
use

218
00:06:11,886 --> 00:06:13,751
has to reach the tissue
all

219
00:06:13,751 --> 00:06:15,541
the way around the joint,

220
00:06:15,541 --> 00:06:17,187
wherever it's being
squeezed.

221
00:06:17,445 --> 00:06:18,628
Is it the stairs?

222
00:06:18,778 --> 00:06:20,240
Is it getting out of the
car?

223
00:06:20,515 --> 00:06:21,391
Is it lying in bed

224
00:06:21,391 --> 00:06:22,604
at three in the morning?

225
00:06:22,778 --> 00:06:23,886
Or standing at the counter

226
00:06:23,886 --> 00:06:25,215
long enough to cook
dinner?

227
00:06:25,462 --> 00:06:27,518
The same swollen tissue is
behind all

228
00:06:27,518 --> 00:06:29,130
of it, which is why
calming

229
00:06:29,130 --> 00:06:30,614
it is the one thing that
can

230
00:06:30,614 --> 00:06:32,365
help with every one of
them.

231
00:06:32,634 --> 00:06:34,018
So that is why calming

232
00:06:34,018 --> 00:06:35,929
the tissue is so
important.

233
00:06:36,317 --> 00:06:38,003
But it's also why getting
real

234
00:06:38,003 --> 00:06:39,659
help for it has been

235
00:06:39,659 --> 00:06:41,534
so expensive for so long.

236
00:06:42,153 --> 00:06:42,879
In most cases,

237
00:06:42,879 --> 00:06:45,257
it's not even covered by
insurance,

238
00:06:45,257 --> 00:06:46,249
so you have to pay

239
00:06:46,249 --> 00:06:47,333
out of your own

240
00:06:47,333 --> 00:06:48,693
pocket, session after
session.

241
00:06:48,993 --> 00:06:50,887
Because the thing that's
been studied

242
00:06:50,887 --> 00:06:53,362
for calming this kind of
irritated

243
00:06:53,362 --> 00:06:55,902
tissue is red and
near-infrared light.

244
00:06:56,226 --> 00:06:58,115
Most of the technology in
a red

245
00:06:58,115 --> 00:06:59,461
light is quite simple.

246
00:06:59,645 --> 00:07:01,964
The tiny lights themselves
are easy

247
00:07:01,964 --> 00:07:03,081
and cheap to make.

248
00:07:03,366 --> 00:07:05,879
That's why there are
billions of them

249
00:07:05,879 --> 00:07:08,077
in phones and TVs around
the world.

250
00:07:08,299 --> 00:07:10,053
But the machines were
expensive.

251
00:07:10,481 --> 00:07:12,204
Professional red light
machines can

252
00:07:12,204 --> 00:07:13,793
cost over fifty thousand
dollars,

253
00:07:13,793 --> 00:07:14,894
so the only

254
00:07:14,894 --> 00:07:16,737
place to get it was a
clinic.

255
00:07:16,777 --> 00:07:17,879
And you had

256
00:07:17,879 --> 00:07:19,140
to go there two

257
00:07:19,140 --> 00:07:20,506
or three times a week

258
00:07:20,506 --> 00:07:21,948
and sit in their chair.

259
00:07:22,252 --> 00:07:24,854
This added a huge amount
of cost,

260
00:07:24,854 --> 00:07:26,540
because everybody had to
get

261
00:07:26,540 --> 00:07:27,656
paid along the way.

262
00:07:27,848 --> 00:07:29,189
Pay for the machine,

263
00:07:29,189 --> 00:07:30,490
pay the clinic,

264
00:07:30,490 --> 00:07:32,234
pay for every session,

265
00:07:32,234 --> 00:07:33,113
pay for the gas

266
00:07:33,113 --> 00:07:35,115
or the ride there and
back,

267
00:07:35,115 --> 00:07:37,263
and pay with your whole
afternoon.

268
00:07:37,611 --> 00:07:38,696
That's a lot of hands

269
00:07:38,696 --> 00:07:39,525
in the pot,

270
00:07:39,525 --> 00:07:40,833
and that's how a single

271
00:07:40,833 --> 00:07:42,690
session of red light at a

272
00:07:42,690 --> 00:07:45,019
clinic now costs about two
hundred dollars.

273
00:07:45,253 --> 00:07:47,084
Three times a week for a

274
00:07:47,084 --> 00:07:48,986
month is twenty-four
hundred dollars.

275
00:07:49,270 --> 00:07:50,805
But that's crazy, isn't
it?

276
00:07:51,306 --> 00:07:52,495
Look how cheap these
